Task: outbox-write atomicity for InventoryStore.reserve (TD-3.3, ADR 0008)

Summary: InventoryStore.reserve's success path (StockReserved) now writes the
matching outbox_events row inside the same session.transaction as its
conditional UPDATE - true atomicity. The InsufficientStock failure path also
writes a StockReservationFailed outbox row (wrapped in the same transaction
block for consistency, though there's no competing state-change write to be
atomic with - 0 rows affected on that path). InventoryNotFound writes no
outbox row (unchanged - caller-input error, not a stock outcome, matches
system-design.md). aggregate_id/correlationId = orderItemId, not sku -
deliberately fixes a drift from the StockEventPublisher this track replaces,
which actually keyed Kafka records by sku despite system-design.md documenting
orderItemId as inventory-events' partition key.

Files changed:
- src/main/scala/inventoryservice/InventoryStore.scala - reserve() signature
  gains orderItemId; writeOutboxEvent helper; both outcome branches now INSERT
  into outbox_events transactionally.
- src/main/scala/inventoryservice/InventoryRoutes.scala - threads req.orderItemId
  (already present on ReserveInventoryRequest) into store.reserve.
- src/test/scala/inventoryservice/InventoryStorePostgresSuite.scala - two new
  tests (success-path atomicity, failure-path outbox row) via raw JDBC read of
  outbox_events; existing reserve() call sites updated for the new parameter.
- src/test/scala/inventoryservice/{InventoryStoreSuite,InventoryRoutesSuite,HealthRoutesSuite}.scala -
  updated fake/in-memory reserve() signatures to match.

Why: ADR 0008 (transactional outbox) - closes TD-3's dual-write hazard for
inventory-service's reserve endpoint; StockEventPublisher's direct Kafka
produce call is replaced in Phase 2/3.

Verification: sbt scalafmtCheck test - 91 passed, 0 failed.
